--save-session <path> now works on both the -p door and the piped-stdin door, including after a failed turn. It's committed as 2c5ad8b2, and clippy, fmt and the full cargo test run all pass.

What it does:
• **Flag:** `--save-session` is added to the known-flags and needs-a-value lists in `src/cli.rs` and parsed into `Config.save_session`. That's +4 lines; the size register now reads 7591 with a Day 216 #978 note.
• **Saving:** save_session_to writes exactly what /save writes (agent.save_messages()). It never creates a missing parent directory.
• **One helper for every exit:** `save_session_after_turn` runs at all six exits after a turn (both stream-json returns, both failed-turn exits in `run_single_prompt`, and the normal end of each door), so the two doors can't drift apart. It calls agent.finish().await before saving, because yoagent's message list is stale until then.
• **Exit codes:** if the save fails, a successful run exits 1 instead of 0, but a turn that already failed keeps its own code. The error reads `error: --save-session: could not write <path>: <reason>`, with both strings sanitized.
• **Not saved:** exits that happen before any turn runs (image read failure, slash-command refusal, empty stdin). There's nothing to resume from.
• Default: without the flag, behaviour is unchanged.

Tests:
• **Unit test:** the save goes through the real writer, the file's bytes equal `save_messages()`, and it reloads through `restore_session_result` with 2 messages. A missing parent dir returns an error and the directory isn't created.
• **Process tests:**
  • (a) `-p` saves a parseable session.
  • (b) piped stdin saves one too.
  • (c) a path under a missing directory exits non-zero, names --save-session on stderr, and the directory isn't created.
  • (d) without the flag: exit 0 and no --save-session text. This one is weak: the test's working directory is deleted after the run, so it can't prove no file was written anywhere.
  • (e) a turn that dies mid-stream still writes the session and still exits non-zero. The existing mid-stream failure fixture made this cheap to add.
• **Positive control:** I disabled the piped door's save call (marked `NEUTERED`) and restored it in the same command. Exactly `save_session_piped_door_writes_the_session` failed, and the marker is gone.

Docs: the --help line, sessions.md, piped-mode.md, the CHANGELOG and the main.rs entry in ARCHITECTURE.md are all updated.
